# aurutils sync ignore list — install as
# ~/.config/aurutils/sync/ignore
#
# One entry per line. `aur sync -u` skips these packages, so they stay at
# whatever version is currently in the repo.
#
# This is ONLY needed for a pinned old version of a package that also
# exists in the AUR. Packages that are not in the AUR at all (prebuilt
# drops, your own customs) are skipped automatically — do not list them.
#
# Entries may be bare package names or repo-qualified:
#
#   electron25
#   roaring-staging/electron25
#
# A repo-qualified entry names the STAGING repo (REPO_NAME) — that is the
# repo `aur sync -u` operates on. Not the published name (PUBLISH_NAME).
